=== ISSUE ===
Title: Rate-limit retries are too fast, and POSTs are retried on 503 (possible duplicate writes)

- On 429 the client retries after 2-4 s. Lichess asks clients to wait after a 429 (https://lichess.org/page/api-tips: "wait a full minute"), so quick retries can extend the throttle.
- The client retries every method on 503. A 503 can come back for a write Lichess actually completed, so a retried POST (send_message, create_challenge, bulk pairings) could happen twice.
- Where: src/http/client.ts, the retry loop in LichessClient.request.

=== PR ===
Title: fix: back off 10 s doubling on 429, and don't retry POSTs on 503
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- 429: waits 10, 20, 40, 80 s (or a longer Retry-After), then gives up when the next wait would pass 3 minutes. Writes are still retried on 429, since Lichess didn't process them.
- 503: retried only for idempotent methods (GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS).
- Tests use fake timers, so they run instantly.

Commits: test first (4 of the 7 new tests fail on main), then the fix.
